## IT-140 M4 Course Assignment: Pseudocode for Higher/Lower Game

PRINT "Welcome to the higher/lower game, Bella!"

SET min number and max number valid to FALSE

WHILE min number and max number valid is FALSE
    READ min number from user
    READ max number from user

    IF min number is less than max number THEN
        SET min number and max number valid to TRUE

    ELSE
        PRINT "The lower bound must be less than the upper bound."

GENERATE random number between min number and max number

PRINT prompt to guess a number between min number and max number
READ the users guess

WHILE user guess is not equal to random number

    WHILE user guess is less than min number OR user guess is greater than max number
        PRINT "Incorrect guess. Please enter a number in range."
        READ the users guess

    IF user guess is less than random number THEN
        PRINT "Nope, too low."
        PRINT "Guess another number:"
        READ the users guess

    ELSE IF user guess is greater than random number THEN
        PRINT "Nope, too high."
        PRINT "Guess another number:"
        READ the users guess

PRINT "You got it, Bella!"
